            {
              "id": "nyc-ll144.data-policy",
              "name": "NycLl144DataPolicy",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Publish the data retention policy and data sources"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "6 RCNY § 5-304(d)(1)-(2) requires the employer or agency to post on the employment section of its website the automated employment decision tool's data retention policy, the type of data it collects and the source of that data, together with instructions for making a written request for that information. NYC Admin. Code § 20-871(b)(3) is the enabling provision and sets the thirty-day window for answering such a request."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "6 RCNY § 5-304(d)(1)-(2) requires the employer or agency to post on the employment section of its website the automated employment decision tool's data retention policy, the type of data it collects and the source of that data, together with instructions for making a written request for that information. NYC Admin. Code § 20-871(b)(3) is the enabling provision and sets the thirty-day window for answering such a request.\n\nPublish the retention policy, data types and data sources, plus instructions for a written request, and answer such requests within thirty days.\n\nNYC Local Law 144 6 RCNY § 5-304(d) — Published data retention policy, data types and sources: https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/about/automated-employment-decision-tools.page\nNYC Local Law 144 § 20-871(b)(3) — Enabling provision and the thirty-day response window: https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/about/automated-employment-decision-tools.page",
                "markdown": "**Publish the data retention policy and data sources**\n6 RCNY § 5-304(d)(1)-(2) requires the employer or agency to post on the employment section of its website the automated employment decision tool's data retention policy, the type of data it collects and the source of that data, together with instructions for making a written request for that information. NYC Admin. Code § 20-871(b)(3) is the enabling provision and sets the thirty-day window for answering such a request.\n**How to close it:** Publish the retention policy, data types and data sources, plus instructions for a written request, and answer such requests within thirty days.\n**Citations**\n- [NYC Local Law 144 6 RCNY § 5-304(d) — Published data retention policy, data types and sources](https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/about/automated-employment-decision-tools.page)\n- [NYC Local Law 144 § 20-871(b)(3) — Enabling provision and the thirty-day response window](https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/about/automated-employment-decision-tools.page)\n_In force from 2023-07-05._"
              },
