                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "colorado-admt.adverse-explanation",
              "name": "ColoradoAdmtAdverseExplanation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Explain an adverse outcome within thirty days"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "On an adverse outcome materially influenced by covered ADMT, the deployer must provide within thirty days a plain-language description of the decision and the technology's role in it, a simple process to request more information, and an explanation of the consumer's rights."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "On an adverse outcome materially influenced by covered ADMT, the deployer must provide within thirty days a plain-language description of the decision and the technology's role in it, a simple process to request more information, and an explanation of the consumer's rights.\n\nTrigger an explanation whenever the outcome is adverse, carry the reason codes from the decision log, and start a thirty-day clock.\n\nColorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1703 — Deployer duties — adverse outcome explanation: https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189",
                "markdown": "**Explain an adverse outcome within thirty days**\nOn an adverse outcome materially influenced by covered ADMT, the deployer must provide within thirty days a plain-language description of the decision and the technology's role in it, a simple process to request more information, and an explanation of the consumer's rights.\n**How to close it:** Trigger an explanation whenever the outcome is adverse, carry the reason codes from the decision log, and start a thirty-day clock.\n**Citations**\n- [Colorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1703 — Deployer duties — adverse outcome explanation](https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189)\n_In force from 2027-01-01._"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "compliance",
                  "colorado-admt",
                  "rights",
                  "upcoming"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "colorado-admt.human-review-override",
              "name": "ColoradoAdmtHumanReviewOverride",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Designated reviewers authorised to override"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A deployer must designate trained individuals authorised to override the technology's outcome during human review, and consumers have a right to meaningful human review and reconsideration after an adverse outcome, to the extent commercially reasonable."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A deployer must designate trained individuals authorised to override the technology's outcome during human review, and consumers have a right to meaningful human review and reconsideration after an adverse outcome, to the extent commercially reasonable.\n\nDesignate reviewers, record who they are, and give them an override that is written back to the decision record.\n\nColorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1704 — Deployer duties — designated reviewers: https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189\nColorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1705 — Consumer rights — meaningful human review: https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189",
                "markdown": "**Designated reviewers authorised to override**\nA deployer must designate trained individuals authorised to override the technology's outcome during human review, and consumers have a right to meaningful human review and reconsideration after an adverse outcome, to the extent commercially reasonable.\n**How to close it:** Designate reviewers, record who they are, and give them an override that is written back to the decision record.\n**Citations**\n- [Colorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1704 — Deployer duties — designated reviewers](https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189)\n- [Colorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1705 — Consumer rights — meaningful human review](https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189)\n_In force from 2027-01-01._"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "compliance",
                  "colorado-admt",
                  "human-oversight",
                  "upcoming"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "colorado-admt.data-correction",
              "name": "ColoradoAdmtDataCorrection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Right to see and correct the data used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A consumer has the right to request the personal data used in the decision and to correct factually incorrect or materially inaccurate data."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A consumer has the right to request the personal data used in the decision and to correct factually incorrect or materially inaccurate data.\n\nExpose the inputs that drove the decision and accept corrections. This is also the cheapest accuracy improvement available: the affected person is usually the only party who knows the data is wrong.\n\nColorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1705 — Consumer rights — access and correction: https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189",
                "markdown": "**Right to see and correct the data used**\nA consumer has the right to request the personal data used in the decision and to correct factually incorrect or materially inaccurate data.\n**How to close it:** Expose the inputs that drove the decision and accept corrections. This is also the cheapest accuracy improvement available: the affected person is usually the only party who knows the data is wrong.\n**Citations**\n- [Colorado ADMT Act § 6-1-1705 — Consumer rights — access and correction](https://leg.colorado.gov/bills/sb26-189)\n_In force from 2027-01-01._"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "compliance",
